# The reference application builds with the repository root as its context
# (sample/go.mod replaces the library and both storage adapters with sibling
# directories), so everything below is reachable from a container build and
# has to be kept out deliberately.

# A go.work is a local development convenience and, during a release, a
# generated file that pins the storage adapters. Either way it names a member
# set that does not include sample/, so a build that sees it fails with
# "directory prefix . does not contain modules listed in go.work" — on the
# release commit, and only there, which is the worst time to find out.
go.work
go.work.sum

.git
.github
backup
conformance
tools/conformance
